---
layout: base.njk
pageTitle: "Antalya Hotel Guide — Compare Areas & Places to Stay"
pageDescription: "Explore 100 sourced hotel profiles across Antalya city, Kaleiçi, Lara, Belek, Kemer, Side, Alanya, Kaş and Kalkan. Filter by area and stay style."
pageUrl: "/hotels/"
permalink: "/hotels/index.html"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{% from 'ui.njk' import icon, rowCard, pageHero, sectionHead %}
{{ pageHero(editorialPhotos | photoById('rixos-belek-2015-2'), 'Places to stay', 'Where to stay in Antalya', collections.hotels.length + ' hotels · 10 areas · resorts, boutique & city stays', [{label: 'Places to stay'}]) }}

<section class="intro-band" aria-label="Choosing an area">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="intro-card" data-readmore>
      <div class="intro-text" id="hotels-intro">
        <p>Choosing the right area matters more than choosing the right hotel. <strong>Kaleiçi</strong> puts you inside the old walls, <strong>Konyaaltı</strong> on the city beach promenade and <strong>Lara</strong> on long sandy resort beaches east of the centre.</p>
        <p><strong>Belek</strong> is the golf coast, with big all-inclusive resorts set among pine forest. <strong>Kemer</strong> sits under the mountains to the west, <strong>Side</strong> mixes beach days with ancient ruins, and <strong>Alanya</strong>, <strong>Kaş</strong> and <strong>Kalkan</strong> are further along the coast — plan transfers separately.</p>
        <p>Each profile links to the hotel’s official website. Prices, availability and seasonal facilities are not live — always confirm your dates, meal plan, cancellation terms and transfers directly with the hotel.</p>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="readmore-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="hotels-intro" hidden>Read more</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="directory" id="hotel-directory" aria-labelledby="directory-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Find your base</p><h2 id="directory-heading">Discover Antalya hotels</h2></div></div>
    <form id="hotel-filters" class="toolbar" hidden aria-label="Filter hotels">
      <div class="search-pill">{{ icon('search') }}<label class="sr-only" for="hotel-search">Hotel name or keyword</label><input type="search" id="hotel-search" name="q" placeholder="I’m looking for… (try Kaleiçi, golf or Akra)" autocomplete="off"></div>
      <div class="filter-row">
        <label for="hotel-area">Area</label>
        <select id="hotel-area" name="area" class="select-pill"><option value="">All areas</option>{% for area in collections.hotels | uniqueValues('neighborhood') %}<option value="{{ area | escape }}">{{ area }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>
        <label for="hotel-type">Style</label>
        <select id="hotel-type" name="type" class="select-pill"><option value="">All styles</option>{% for type in ["City hotel", "Boutique & heritage", "Coastal resort", "Golf resort"] %}<option value="{{ type | escape }}">{{ type }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>
        <button type="reset" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline">Reset filters</button>
      </div>
    </form>
    <noscript><p>All hotels are listed below. Use your browser’s Find command to search a name or area.</p></noscript>
    <p id="hotel-results" class="results-count" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Showing {{ collections.hotels.length }} hotels</p>
    <div class="row-list">
      {% for hotel in collections.hotels %}
      {% set hotelSlug = hotel.data.slug or (hotel.data.title | slugify) %}
      {% set ph = hotel.data | cardPhoto(editorialPhotos) %}
      {% set attrs = ' data-hotel data-area="' + (hotel.data.neighborhood | escape) + '" data-type="' + (hotel.data.category | escape) + '"' %}
      {{ rowCard('/hotels/' + hotelSlug + '/', ph, hotel.data.title, hotel.data.excerpt, [{icon: 'pin', label: hotel.data.neighborhood}, {icon: 'bed', label: hotel.data.category}], ('Golf' if hotel.data.category == 'Golf resort' else ''), attrs) }}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div id="hotel-empty" class="hotel-empty" hidden><h3>No hotels match these filters</h3><p>Try a broader keyword, choose another area or reset your filters.</p><button type="button" id="hotel-reset-empty" class="btn btn-orange">Show all hotels</button></div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="/js/hotels.js" defer></script>
